    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12266" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">daemŏnĭăcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαιμονιακός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to an evil spirit, demoniac,
			devilish</i> (eccl. Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">potentia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 15</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">daemoniacus</span></b> , i, m., <i>a demoniac, one possessed by an evil spirit</i>,
			Firm. Math. 3, 6; Sulpic. Sever. Vit. S. <i><span class="en">Mart.
			18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
